{"id":"mahabharata-8-032","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":32,"title":"द्वात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 32 · The great battle of the seventeenth day","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how the armies arrayed and fought against the Samshaptakas, and Sanjaya describes the clash with omens and portents on earth and sky. Nakula fights Karna's son and the great armies come together again.","kn":"ಸಂಶಪ್ತಕರ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಹೇಗೆ ಜೋಡಿಸಿ ಹೋರಾಡಿದವೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೂಮಿ ಆಕಾಶದ ಅಪಶಕುನಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಘರ್ಷವನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಕುಲ ಕರ್ಣಪುತ್ರನೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಮಹಾಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಮತ್ತೆ ಸೇರುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि संशप्तकों के विरुद्ध सेनाओं ने कैसे व्यूह बनाकर युद्ध किया, और संजय पृथ्वी-आकाश के अपशकुनों के साथ संघर्ष का वर्णन करते हैं। नकुल कर्ण के पुत्र से लड़ता है और विशाल सेनाएँ फिर मिलती हैं।","te":"సంశప్తకులకు వ్యతిరేకంగా సేనలు ఎలా వ్యూహంగా నిలిచి పోరాడాయని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు; భూమి ఆకాశంలోని దుశ్శకునాలతో పోరును సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. నకులుడు కర్ణపుత్రునితో పోరాడతాడు; మహాసేనలు మళ్లీ కలుస్తాయి.","ta":"சம்சப்தகருக்கு எதிராகப் படைகள் எவ்வாறு அணிவகுத்துப் போரிட்டன என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்க, மண்ணிலும் விண்ணிலும் துர்நிமித்தங்களுடன் மோதலைச் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான். நகுலன் கர்ணனின் மகனுடன் போரிட, பெரும்படைகள் மீண்டும் கூடுகின்றன.","ml":"സംശപ്തകർക്കെതിരെ സേനകൾ എങ്ങനെ അണിനിരന്നു, എങ്ങനെ പൊരുതി എന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ഭൂമിയിലും ആകാശത്തും ദുശ്ശകുനങ്ങളോടെ നടന്ന പോരാട്ടം സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. പതിനേഴാം ദിവസത്തെ മഹായുദ്ധത്തിൽ നകുലൻ കർണ്ണന്റെ പുത്രനോട് പൊരുതുന്നു; മഹാസേനകൾ വീണ്ടും ഒന്നിച്ചുചേരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.32; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा व्यूढेष्वनीकेषु संसक्तेषु च संजय ।\nसंशप्तकान्कथं पार्थो गतः कर्णश्च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, with the armies arrayed and engaged in this way, how did Partha go against the Samshaptakas, and Karna against the Pandavas?"}},{"n":2,"text":"एतद्विस्तरतो युद्धं प्रब्रूहि कुशलो ह्यसि ।\nन हि तृप्यामि वीराणां शृण्वानो विक्रमान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me this battle in detail, for you are skilled; I am never satisfied with hearing of the heroes' prowess in battle."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्स्थाने समवस्थाप्य प्रत्यमित्रं महाबलम् ।\nअव्यूहतार्जुनो व्यूहं पुत्रस्य तव दुर्नये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having placed the mighty enemy in position, Arjuna then drew up an array against your son's ill-judged array."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्सादिनागकलिलं पदातिरथसंकुलम् ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नमुखैर्व्यूढमशोभत महद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great force, crowded with cavalry and elephants, thick with infantry and chariots, shone as arrayed by Dhrishtadyumna and the others."}},{"n":5,"text":"पारावतसवर्णाश्वश्चन्द्रादित्यसमद्युतिः ।\nपार्षतः प्रबभौ धन्वी कालो विग्रहवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prishata's son, with horses the color of doves and radiance like the moon and sun, shone as a bowman, like Death embodied."}},{"n":6,"text":"पार्षतं त्वभि संतस्थुर्द्रौपदेया युयुत्सवः ।\nसानुगा भीमवपुषश्चन्द्रं तारागणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Around Prishata's son stood Draupadi's sons with their followers, eager to fight, terrible in form, like the host of stars around the moon."}},{"n":7,"text":"अथ व्यूढेष्वनीकेषु प्रेक्ष्य संशप्तकान्रणे ।\nक्रुद्धोऽर्जुनोऽभिदुद्राव व्याक्षिपन्गाण्डिवं धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, the armies drawn up, Arjuna, seeing the Samshaptakas in battle, rushed at them in anger, twanging the Gandiva bow."}},{"n":8,"text":"अथ संशप्तकाः पार्थमभ्यधावन्वधैषिणः ।\nविजये कृतसंकल्पा मृत्युं कृत्वा निवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Samshaptakas, wishing to kill, ran at Partha, resolved on victory, making death their return."}},{"n":9,"text":"तदश्वसंघबहुलं मत्तनागरथाकुलम् ।\nपत्तिमच्छूरवीरौघैर्द्रुतमर्जुनमाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That force, full of hosts of horses and crowded with rutting elephants and chariots, with infantry and floods of brave heroes, swiftly rushed at Arjuna."}},{"n":10,"text":"स संप्रहारस्तुमुलस्तेषामासीत्किरीटिना ।\nतस्यैव नः श्रुतो यादृङ्निवातकवचैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fierce clash of those men with Kiritin was such as we heard of his fight with the Nivatakavachas."}},{"n":11,"text":"रथानश्वान्ध्वजान्नागान्पत्तीन्रथपतीनपि ।\nइषून्धनूंषि खड्गांश्च चक्राणि च परश्वधान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha cut off chariots, horses, banners, elephants, foot soldiers and chariot-lords, arrows, bows, swords, discuses and axes,"}},{"n":12,"text":"सायुधानुद्यतान्बाहूनुद्यतान्यायुधानि च ।\nचिच्छेद द्विषतां पार्थः शिरांसि च सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"raised arms with weapons and raised weapons, and the heads of his foes by thousands."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्मिन्सैन्ये महावर्ते पातालावर्तसंनिभे ।\nनिमग्नं तं रथं मत्वा नेदुः संशप्तका मुदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking that chariot sunk in that army like a great whirlpool, like the whirlpools of the netherworld, the Samshaptakas roared in joy."}},{"n":14,"text":"स पुरस्तादरीन्हत्वा पश्चार्धेनोत्तरेण च ।\nदक्षिणेन च बीभत्सुः क्रुद्धो रुद्रः पशूनिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu, killing foes in front, behind, to the north, south and all around, was like angry Rudra among beasts."}},{"n":15,"text":"अथ पाञ्चालचेदीनां सृञ्जयानां च मारिष ।\nत्वदीयैः सह संग्राम आसीत्परमदारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, sir, a most dreadful battle took place between the Panchalas, Chedis and Srinjayas and your men."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृपश्च कृतवर्मा च शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ।\nहृष्टसेनाः सुसंरब्धा रथानीकैः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, Kritavarman and Shakuni son of Subala, with delighted armies and great fury, struck with their chariot divisions."}},{"n":17,"text":"कोसलैः काशिमत्स्यैश्च कारूषैः केकयैरपि ।\nशूरसेनैः शूरवीरैर्युयुधुर्युद्धदुर्मदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maddened for battle, they fought with the Kosalas, Kashis, Matsyas, Karushas, Kekayas and the heroic Shurasenas."}},{"n":18,"text":"तेषामन्तकरं युद्धं देहपाप्मप्रणाशनम् ।\nशूद्रविट्क्षत्रवीराणां धर्म्यं स्वर्ग्यं यशस्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That battle was the end for them, destroying the sins of the body, righteous and heaven-giving and glory-bringing for heroes of the shudra, vaishya and kshatriya classes."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्योधनोऽपि सहितो भ्रातृभिर्भरतर्षभ ।\nगुप्तः कुरुप्रवीरैश्च मद्राणां च महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, bull of the Bharatas, together with his brothers and guarded by the Kuru heroes and the great warriors of the Madras,"}},{"n":20,"text":"पाण्डवैः सहपाञ्चालैश्चेदिभिः सात्यकेन च ।\nयुध्यमानं रणे कर्णं कुरुवीरोऽभ्यपालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Kuru hero protected Karna, who was fighting in the battle against the Pandavas with the Panchalas, Chedis and Satyaki."}},{"n":21,"text":"कर्णोऽपि निशितैर्बाणैर्विनिहत्य महाचमूम् ।\nप्रमृद्य च रथश्रेष्ठान्युधिष्ठिरमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna too, smashing the great army with sharp arrows and crushing the best chariot-fighters, pressed Yudhishthira hard."}},{"n":22,"text":"विपत्रायुधदेहासून्कृत्वा शत्रून्सहस्रशः ।\nयुक्त्वा स्वर्गयशोभ्यां च स्वेभ्यो मुदमुदावहत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made thousands of foes lose their weapons, bodies and lives, and having joined them to heaven and glory, he brought joy to his own men."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"यत्तत्प्रविश्य पार्थानां सेनां कुर्वञ्जनक्षयम् ।\nकर्णो राजानमभ्यर्च्छत्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, tell me how Karna, entering the Pandavas' army and slaughtering its people, attacked the king."}},{"n":24,"text":"के च प्रवीराः पार्थानां युधि कर्णमवारयन् ।\nकांश्च प्रमथ्याधिरथिर्युधिष्ठिरमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Which heroes of the Pandavas held Karna back in the battle, and whom did Adhiratha's son crush to press Yudhishthira?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नमुखान्पार्थान्दृष्ट्वा कर्णो व्यवस्थितान् ।\nसमभ्यधावत्त्वरितः पाञ्चालाञ्शत्रुकर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas positioned with Dhrishtadyumna at the head, Karna, tormentor of foes, quickly rushed at the Panchalas."}},{"n":26,"text":"तं तूर्णमभिधावन्तं पाञ्चाला जितकाशिनः ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुर्महाराज हंसा इव महार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he rushed swiftly, the Panchalas, who were victorious over the Kashis, went out to meet him, great king, like swans to the great ocean."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः शङ्खसहस्राणां निस्वनो हृदयंगमः ।\nप्रादुरासीदुभयतो भेरीशब्दश्च दारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a heart-stirring sound of thousands of conches arose, and a dreadful sound of kettledrums from both sides."}},{"n":28,"text":"नानावादित्रनादश्च द्विपाश्वरथनिस्वनः ।\nसिंहनादश्च वीराणामभवद्दारुणस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There came the din of many instruments and of elephants, horses and chariots, and the dreadful lion-roar of the heroes."}},{"n":29,"text":"साद्रिद्रुमार्णवा भूमिः सवाताम्बुदमम्बरम् ।\nसार्केन्दुग्रहनक्षत्रा द्यौश्च व्यक्तं व्यघूर्णत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth with its mountains, trees and oceans, the sky with winds and clouds, and the heavens with sun, moon, planets and stars visibly whirled."}},{"n":30,"text":"अति भूतानि तं शब्दं मेनिरेऽति च विव्यथुः ।\nयानि चाप्लवसत्त्वानि प्रायस्तानि मृतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creatures thought that sound excessive and were greatly pained, and most of the creatures that live in water died."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथ कर्णो भृशं क्रुद्धः शीघ्रमस्त्रमुदीरयन् ।\nजघान पाण्डवीं सेनामासुरीं मघवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, greatly angry, swiftly launching his weapons, struck down the Pandava army like Indra striking the asuras."}},{"n":32,"text":"स पाण्डवरथांस्तूर्णं प्रविश्य विसृजञ्शरान् ।\nप्रभद्रकाणां प्रवरानहनत्सप्तसप्ततिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quickly entering the Pandava chariots, loosing arrows, he killed seventy-seven of the best of the Prabhadrakas."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः सुपुङ्खैर्निशितै रथश्रेष्ठो रथेषुभिः ।\nअवधीत्पञ्चविंशत्या पाञ्चालान्पञ्चविंशतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that best of charioteers, with sharp, well-feathered chariot arrows, killed twenty-five Panchalas with twenty-five arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"सुवर्णपुङ्खैर्नाराचैः परकायविदारणैः ।\nचेदिकानवधीद्वीरः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With golden-feathered iron arrows that tear the enemy's bodies, the hero killed Chedis by hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":35,"text":"तं तथा समरे कर्म कुर्वाणमतिमानुषम् ।\nपरिवव्रुर्महाराज पाञ्चालानां रथव्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he did superhuman deeds so in the battle, great king, the chariot-throngs of the Panchalas surrounded him."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः संधाय विशिखान्पञ्च भारत दुःसहान् ।\nपाञ्चालानवधीत्पञ्च कर्णो वैकर्तनो वृषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna Vaikartana, the Vrisha, fitting five unbearable arrows, killed five Panchalas, Bharata."}},{"n":37,"text":"भानुदेवं चित्रसेनं सेनाबिन्दुं च भारत ।\nतपनं शूरसेनं च पाञ्चालानवधीद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhanudeva, Chitrasena, Senabindu, Tapana and Shurasena: these Panchalas he killed in battle."}},{"n":38,"text":"पाञ्चालेषु च शूरेषु वध्यमानेषु सायकैः ।\nहाहाकारो महानासीत्पाञ्चालानां महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the brave Panchalas were being cut down by arrows, a great cry of \"Alas, alas!\" arose among the Panchalas in that great battle."}},{"n":39,"text":"तेषां संकीर्यमाणानां हाहाकारकृता दिशः ।\nपुनरेव च तान्कर्णो जघानाशु पतत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they were scattered, the directions rang with their cries, and again Karna swiftly killed them with his arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"चक्ररक्षौ तु कर्णस्य पुत्रौ मारिष दुर्जयौ ।\nसुषेणः सत्यसेनश्च त्यक्त्वा प्राणानयुध्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two sons of Karna, hard to conquer, Sushena and Satyasena, guards of his wheels, fought regardless of life, sir."}},{"n":41,"text":"पृष्ठगोपस्तु कर्णस्य ज्येष्ठः पुत्रो महारथः ।\nवृषसेनः स्वयं कर्णं पृष्ठतः पर्यपालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna's eldest son, the great warrior Vrishasena, himself guarded Karna from behind as his rear protector."}},{"n":42,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः सात्यकिश्च द्रौपदेया वृकोदरः ।\nजनमेजयः शिखण्डी च प्रवीराश्च प्रभद्रकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, Satyaki, Draupadi's sons, Vrikodara, Janamejaya, Shikhandi and the Prabhadraka heroes,"}},{"n":43,"text":"चेदिकेकयपाञ्चाला यमौ मत्स्याश्च दंशिताः ।\nसमभ्यधावन्राधेयं जिघांसन्तः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Chedis, Kekayas, Panchalas, the twins and the Matsyas, armored, rushed at Radheya, fighting, wanting to kill him."}},{"n":44,"text":"त एनं विविधैः शस्त्रैः शरधाराभिरेव च ।\nअभ्यवर्षन्विमृद्नन्तः प्रावृषीवाम्बुदा गिरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They rained on him with various weapons and streams of arrows, crushing him, like clouds in the rainy season on a mountain."}},{"n":45,"text":"पितरं तु परीप्सन्तः कर्णपुत्राः प्रहारिणः ।\nत्वदीयाश्चापरे राजन्वीरा वीरानवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna's sons, striking, wishing to protect their father, and other heroes of yours, king, held back those heroes."}},{"n":46,"text":"सुषेणो भीमसेनस्य छित्त्वा भल्लेन कार्मुकम् ।\nनाराचैः सप्तभिर्विद्ध्वा हृदि भीमं ननाद ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sushena cut Bhimasena's bow with a broad-headed arrow, pierced Bhima in the chest with seven iron arrows and roared."}},{"n":47,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सुदृढं भीमविक्रमः ।\nसज्यं वृकोदरः कृत्वा सुषेणस्याच्छिनद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vrikodara, of terrible prowess, took another very strong bow, strung it, and cut Sushena's bow."}},{"n":48,"text":"विव्याध चैनं नवभिः क्रुद्धो नृत्यन्निवेषुभिः ।\nकर्णं च तूर्णं विव्याध त्रिसप्तत्या शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angry, he pierced him with nine arrows as if dancing, and quickly pierced Karna with seventy-three sharp arrows."}},{"n":49,"text":"सत्यसेनं च दशभिः साश्वसूतध्वजायुधम् ।\nपश्यतां सुहृदां मध्ये कर्णपुत्रमपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And with ten arrows he felled Karna's son Satyasena together with horses, charioteer, banner and weapons, as his friends watched."}},{"n":50,"text":"क्षुरप्रणुन्नं तत्तस्य शिरश्चन्द्रनिभाननम् ।\nशुभदर्शनमेवासीन्नालभ्रष्टमिवाम्बुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That head, struck by a razor-arrow, with a face like the moon, was beautiful to see, like a lotus fallen from its stalk."}},{"n":51,"text":"हत्वा कर्णसुतं भीमस्तावकान्पुनरार्दयत् ।\nकृपहार्दिक्ययोश्छित्त्वा चापे तावप्यथार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Karna's son, Bhima again harassed your men; he cut the bows of Kripa and Hardikya, and then harassed those two."}},{"n":52,"text":"दुःशासनं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा शकुनिं षड्भिरायसैः ।\nउलूकं च पतत्रिं च चकार विरथावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Dushasana with three iron arrows and Shakuni with six, and made Ulûka and Patri both chariotless."}},{"n":53,"text":"हे सुषेण हतोऽसीति ब्रुवन्नादत्त सायकम् ।\nतमस्य कर्णश्चिच्छेद त्रिभिश्चैनमताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"Sushena, you are dead!\" he took up an arrow; Karna cut it and struck Bhima with three."}},{"n":54,"text":"अथान्यमपि जग्राह सुपर्वाणं सुतेजनम् ।\nसुषेणायासृजद्भीमस्तमप्यस्याच्छिनद्वृषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima then took another, with good joints and great sharpness, and shot it at Sushena; Vrisha cut that too."}},{"n":55,"text":"पुनः कर्णस्त्रिसप्तत्या भीमसेनं रथेषुभिः ।\nपुत्रं परीप्सन्विव्याध क्रूरं क्रूरैर्जिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again Karna, wishing to protect his son, pierced the cruel Bhimasena with seventy-three chariot arrows, wanting to kill him with cruel ones."}},{"n":56,"text":"सुषेणस्तु धनुर्गृह्य भारसाधनमुत्तमम् ।\nनकुलं पञ्चभिर्बाणैर्बाह्वोरुरसि चार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sushena took up an excellent bow able to bear strain and hit Nakula in the arms and chest with five arrows."}},{"n":57,"text":"नकुलस्तं तु विंशत्या विद्ध्वा भारसहैर्दृढैः ।\nननाद बलवन्नादं कर्णस्य भयमादधत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula pierced him with twenty strong, burden-bearing arrows and gave a mighty roar, bringing fear to Karna."}},{"n":58,"text":"तं सुषेणो महाराज विद्ध्वा दशभिराशुगैः ।\nचिच्छेद च धनुः शीघ्रं क्षुरप्रेण महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, Sushena, a great warrior, pierced him with ten swift arrows and quickly cut his bow with a razor-arrow."}},{"n":59,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय नकुलः क्रोधमूर्च्छितः ।\nसुषेणं बहुभिर्बाणैर्वारयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Nakula, swooning with rage, took another bow and checked Sushena in battle with many arrows."}},{"n":60,"text":"स तु बाणैर्दिशो राजन्नाच्छाद्य परवीरहा ।\nआजघ्ने सारथिं चास्य सुषेणं च ततस्त्रिभिः ।\nचिच्छेद चास्य सुदृढं धनुर्भल्लैस्त्रिभिस्त्रिधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covering the directions with arrows, that slayer of enemy heroes, king, struck Sushena's charioteer and Sushena with three more, and cut his strong bow in three with three broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":61,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सुषेणः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nअविध्यन्नकुलं षष्ट्या सहदेवं च सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sushena, swooning with rage, took another bow and pierced Nakula with sixty arrows and Sahadeva with seven."}},{"n":62,"text":"तद्युद्धं सुमहद्घोरमासीद्देवासुरोपमम् ।\nनिघ्नतां सायकैस्तूर्णमन्योन्यस्य वधं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That very great and terrible fight was like that of gods and asuras, as they swiftly struck each other with arrows, seeking each other's death."}},{"n":63,"text":"सात्यकिर्वृषसेनस्य हत्वा सूतं त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन जघानाश्वांश्च सप्तभिः ।\nध्वजमेकेषुणोन्मथ्य त्रिभिस्तं हृद्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki killed Vrishasena's charioteer with three arrows, cut his bow with a broad-head, killed his horses with seven, smashed his banner with one, and struck him in the chest with three."}},{"n":64,"text":"अथावसन्नः स्वरथे मुहूर्तात्पुनरुत्थितः ।\nअथो जिघांसुः शैनेयं खड्गचर्मभृदभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sunk in his chariot, but risen again after a moment, Vrishasena, wanting to kill the Shini's descendant, came up with sword and shield."}},{"n":65,"text":"तस्य चाप्लवतः शीघ्रं वृषसेनस्य सात्यकिः ।\nवराहकर्णैर्दशभिरविध्यदसिचर्मणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Vrishasena rushed up quickly, Satyaki pierced his sword and shield with ten boar-eared arrows."}},{"n":66,"text":"दुःशासनस्तु तं दृष्ट्वा विरथं व्यायुधं कृतम् ।\nआरोप्य स्वरथे तूर्णमपोवाह रथान्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him chariotless and weaponless, Dushasana quickly put him in his own chariot and carried him to another chariot."}},{"n":67,"text":"अथान्यं रथमास्थाय वृषसेनो महारथः ।\nकर्णस्य युधि दुर्धर्षः पुनः पृष्ठमपालयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vrishasena, great warrior, mounting another chariot, hard to overcome in the battle, again guarded Karna's rear."}},{"n":68,"text":"दुःशासनं तु शैनेयो नवैर्नवभिराशुगैः ।\nविसूताश्वरथं कृत्वा ललाटे त्रिभिरार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Shini's descendant, with nine times nine swift arrows, made Dushasana lose his charioteer, horses and chariot, and struck him with three on the forehead."}},{"n":69,"text":"स त्वन्यं रथमास्थाय विधिवत्कल्पितं पुनः ।\nयुयुधे पाण्डुभिः सार्धं कर्णस्याप्याययन्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dushasana mounted another chariot, duly prepared, and again fought with the Pandavas, adding to Karna's strength."}},{"n":70,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्ततः कर्णमविध्यद्दशभिः शरैः ।\nद्रौपदेयास्त्रिसप्तत्या युयुधानस्तु सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhrishtadyumna pierced Karna with ten arrows, Draupadi's sons with seventy-three, Yuyudhana with seven,"}},{"n":71,"text":"भीमसेनश्चतुःषष्ट्या सहदेवश्च पञ्चभिः ।\nनकुलस्त्रिंशता बाणैः शतानीकश्च सप्तभिः ।\nशिखण्डी दशभिर्वीरो धर्मराजः शतेन तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena with sixty-four, Sahadeva with five, Nakula with thirty, Shatanika with seven, the hero Shikhandi with ten, and the king of dharma with a hundred."}},{"n":72,"text":"एते चान्ये च राजेन्द्र प्रवीरा जयगृद्धिनः ।\nअभ्यर्दयन्महेष्वासं सूतपुत्रं महामृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and other heroes, king of kings, eager for victory, harassed the great bowman, the charioteer's son, in that great battle."}},{"n":73,"text":"तान्सूतपुत्रो विशिखैर्दशभिर्दशभिः शितैः ।\nरथे चारु चरन्वीरः प्रत्यविध्यदरिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The charioteer's son, hero and subduer of foes, moving gracefully in his chariot, pierced each of them back with ten sharp arrows."}},{"n":74,"text":"तत्रास्त्रवीर्यं कर्णस्य लाघवं च महात्मनः ।\nअपश्याम महाराज तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, great king, we saw the weapon-power and lightness of the great-souled Karna; it was wondrous."}},{"n":75,"text":"न ह्याददानं ददृशुः संदधानं च सायकान् ।\nविमुञ्चन्तं च संरम्भाद्ददृशुस्ते महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not see him take up or fit arrows, but saw only that great warrior releasing them in fury."}},{"n":76,"text":"द्यौर्वियद्भूर्दिशश्चाशु प्रणुन्ना निशितैः शरैः ।\nअरुणाभ्रावृताकारं तस्मिन्देशे बभौ वियत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sky, space, earth and the directions were quickly filled with his sharp arrows; there the sky seemed covered with a dawn-red cloud."}},{"n":77,"text":"नृत्यन्निव हि राधेयश्चापहस्तः प्रतापवान् ।\nयैर्विद्धः प्रत्यविध्यत्तानेकैकं त्रिगुणैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glorious Radheya, bow in hand, seemed to dance; whoever hit him, he hit back each with three times as many arrows."}},{"n":78,"text":"दशभिर्दशभिश्चैनान्पुनर्विद्ध्वा ननाद ह ।\nसाश्वसूतध्वजच्छत्रास्ततस्ते विवरं ददुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Piercing them again with ten each, he roared; with horses, charioteers, banners and parasols, they gave way."}},{"n":79,"text":"तान्प्रमृद्नन्महेष्वासान्राधेयः शरवृष्टिभिः ।\nराजानीकमसंबाधं प्राविशच्छत्रुकर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crushing those great bowmen with showers of arrows, Radheya, tormentor of foes, entered the unobstructed royal army."}},{"n":80,"text":"स रथांस्त्रिशतान्हत्वा चेदीनामनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nराधेयो निशितैर्बाणैस्ततोऽभ्यार्च्छद्युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed three hundred of the unretreating Chedi chariot warriors with sharp arrows, Radheya then attacked Yudhishthira."}},{"n":81,"text":"ततस्ते पाण्डवा राजञ्शिखण्डी च ससात्यकिः ।\nराधेयात्परिरक्षन्तो राजानं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, the Pandavas, with Shikhandi and Satyaki, protecting the king from Radheya, surrounded him."}},{"n":82,"text":"तथैव तावकाः सर्वे कर्णं दुर्वारणं रणे ।\nयत्ताः सेनामहेष्वासाः पर्यरक्षन्त सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise all your great bowmen eagerly protected the army and Karna, hard to hold back in battle, on every side."}},{"n":83,"text":"नानावादित्रघोषाश्च प्रादुरासन्विशां पते ।\nसिंहनादश्च संजज्ञे शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sounds of many instruments arose, lord of men, and the lion-roar of the unretreating heroes."}},{"n":84,"text":"ततः पुनः समाजग्मुरभीताः कुरुपाण्डवाः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरमुखाः पार्थाः सूतपुत्रमुखा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the fearless Kurus and Pandavas came together again, the Pandavas led by Yudhishthira and we by the charioteer's son."}}]}]}